{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"The strict artifact check passed. Its later trailer head differs from the sealed checkout only in three derived index files, which I verified directly.\n\nI’m requesting changes for the deleted-dependency and malformed-metadata cases. The four findings listed in the generated previous-round section are fixed. No repository files changed, and no attestation was recorded.\n"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThe four previous findings are fixed. Two further blockers remain:\n\n- **N5 — high:** [validate_scope.go:140](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1106239546/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:140). Deleting a dependency’s directory or manifest removes it from current module discovery. Its deleted paths become unmapped, self-contained dependents are exempted, and dependency propagation never selects them. For example, `b` with `selfContained: true`, `dependsOn: [\"a\"]`, and a check reading `../a/input.txt` can retain its old pass after deleting `a`. Preserve dependency ownership across deletions or conservatively rerun affected consumers.\n- **N6 — medium:** [validate_scope.go:42](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1106239546/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:42). Metadata decoding errors are discarded. A record containing `\"selfContained\": true, \"dependsOn\": \"a\"` can retain the exemption while losing its dependency edge. Changes to `a` can then carry `b` silently. Reject invalid metadata or fall back to full validation.\n\nBoth findings follow from code inspection; writable scratch was unavailable for additional fixtures.\n\nFocused tests, race tests and vet passed. Strict artifact-check passed; its later head differs only in three derived indexes. Both required validation runs failed because the sandbox denied build-directory/cache writes. The supplied sealed matrix records 236 passes, but fresh required-tool validation remains unmet.\n\nApplied the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N5\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 140,\n      \"summary\": \"Deleting a dependency directory or its manifest removes that module from current discovery. Its deleted paths become unmapped, selfContained dependents are exempted, and dependency propagation cannot find the removed module in Selected. A dependent check reading the deleted module can therefore retain its old pass. Preserve base/dependency ownership for deletions or conservatively select affected consumers; cover directory and manifest removal under both flags.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N6\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 42,\n      \"summary\": \"loadScopeMetadata discards JSON decoding errors and returns partially populated metadata. For example, selfContained:true with dependsOn:\\\"a\\\" can retain the exemption while dropping the invalid dependency field, allowing a changed dependency's consumer to be carried silently. Return an actionable error or conservatively run the full matrix when metadata cannot be decoded.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:77 and validate_carry.go:147 use NUL-delimited git diff with --no-renames. TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:140 prevents the root module from claiming the unmapped-file exemption. TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:86-98 splits tracked and untracked Git names on NUL without trimming or quoted-name parsing. TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-N4\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:82-85 rejects unverifiable current builds and dirty base identities; engineIdentityFrom returns false for modified builds. TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds passed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the full subject against R1-R10 and D1-D3, including all prior fixes, eligibility, engine identity, dirty-base protection, module discovery, dependency propagation, administrative exclusions, dispatch and cancellation, result accounting, chained origins, delivery freshness consumers, legacy compatibility, documentation and scaffold copies. Focused and broader validation-related tests, race tests and vet passed. Additional findings concern deleted dependencies and invalid metadata. Repository remained unchanged.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified dirty-base and dirty-engine guards and the four prior fixes. Explicit self-containment remains an instance responsibility, but D1 also assumes dependency changes remain discoverable; deletion violates that assumption even with correctly declared edges.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected carried-entry exclusion from worker dispatch, serial accounting and existing cancellation paths. Focused carry, selection and engine-identity race tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive record fields, canonical-output restrictions, legacy parsing and original-head delivery reading. Existing records retain their interpretation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Malformed dependency metadata is silently accepted as partial configuration instead of producing an actionable error or conservative fallback.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A removed provider can disappear from selection before its declared consumers are widened, allowing stale carried outcomes to receive current run provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Normal fallback and selection explanations are useful, but discarded metadata errors leave no diagnostic explaining the lost dependency edge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed optional JSON fields, unchanged legacy parsing, explicit flag combinations and refusal of old bases without engine_version. Changes to CLI and file contracts are additive; no MCP signature changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing regression fixtures pass, but removing a dependency can carry a consumer whose declared inputs changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing affected-module selection addresses repeated full execution. D1's justification for current material provenance nevertheless requires complete dependency invalidation, which fails when a dependency disappears from current discovery.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records original-observation reuse and its unchanged-input premise; D2 and D3 provide engine/matrix comparison and self-containment policy.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared manuals, translations, embedded copies, help, spec and ADR. Carry behavior and prior fixes are documented consistently. The English embedded-copy difference is the repository-specific Contributor Mode section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Invalid metadata can silently narrow execution without naming the decoding failure or offering remediation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R6 requires declared dependency widening, including for self-contained modules. A removed dependency is not propagated. R3 and D1 consequently permit stale carried evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-adcaa66093f2a598\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared implementation, tests, governance and documentation changes against the spec's affected areas and artifact declarations. Changes remain within the approved carry feature.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision confinement and output-path restrictions remain intact, but incomplete dependency invalidation permits stale evidence to acquire current material provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-adcaa66093f2a598\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module selection and whole-matrix comparison is smaller than per-check input manifests or output caching and adds no speculative infrastructure. It remains sufficient only when declared dependencies are completely invalidated and configuration errors cannot narrow execution; N5 and N6 identify the missing conditions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exited 0 with 15 claims, 20 observations and 985 reported findings. Its trailer range ends at 217e24ec; comparison with the sealed checkout showed only delivery-integrity.json, generation.json and spec-graph.json differences.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the supplied sealed structural evidence and inspected the ADR and complete diff. Writable scratch for isolated assessment execution was unavailable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment publication would change files. Scratch creation failed with a read-only filesystem error.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment. Inspected producer, parser and material-freshness consumers directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment; no output was written into the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved and consulted backend-go, security and documentation-style rules; additionally applied delivery-evidence and consumed relevant knowledge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict; it exited 1 with 236 failures because child checks could not create build directories or write caches in the read-only sandbox. The committed canonical record reports 236 passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; it exited 1 with 233 failures caused by sandbox write restrictions. Independent focused and broader validation-related tests, focused race tests and vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
